# `planner --demo` plays a list (crates/mp-gui/src/demo_script.rs; the owner's word of 2026-11-18:
# "i would like this editable-list-of-clicks to be the entire demo"). The demo's own list,
# tools/demo/owner.gui, starts a simulator and flies it; this plays a short one in its place
# through the harness's door, MP_DEMO_FILE - tests/gui/demo-list.steps - with no link and nothing
# fetched: a wait for a control, clicks on tabs, a click and a right click at points of the map, a
# key, an answer to a question that never comes, a pause, and waits for two screens.
#
# The claim: the planner plays it by itself with its drawn pointer, each click a real one - the
# map's click adds a waypoint, the tabs change the screen - in the list's order, to its end, and
# says so; no plugin plays it. Run from the repository as
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/demo-list.gui -- --demo

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 13
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env MP_DEMO_FILE tests/gui/demo-list.steps

expect plugins.count 0
expect demo.script ~ line
within 10
expect demo.pointer shown
within 10
expect screen plan
# The map's click, as a pilot's: a waypoint.
within 10
expect mission.items 1
within 15
expect screen help
within 10
expect demo.script done
expect demo.skipped none
expect screen fly
expect demo.last tab-fly
expect demo.clicks 5
expect vehicle.connected false
